### Right Status Card

Keep this card minimal — do not repeat dates, deadlines, period labels, or progress % (progress lives only on the bottom bar).

Show only two rows inside a dark rounded card with a subtle border/glow:

1. **Month row**
   - small calendar outline icon (accent color)
   - text exactly: `{{ challenge.month_label }}`
   - emphasize the current month number; mute the total

2. **MRR row** (below a thin divider)
   - small coin / currency outline icon
   - text exactly: `Current MRR: {{ content.revenue_label }}`
   - emphasize the MRR amount

Do NOT show:
- start date / deadline
- “PERIOD” month name (e.g. July 2026)
- duplicate “CURRENT PERIOD” blocks
- progress percent or “toward target” copy in this card

### Bottom Progress Bar

Draw a single wide horizontal progress bar as the main bottom graphic (full width within safe margins).

Style:
- capsule / pill track with rounded ends
- dark translucent track, subtle border
- filled portion with a smooth gradient (accent → primary / chart color)
- circular marker (thumb) on the fill edge with a thin light outline
- optional subtle tick marks along the track

Labels (exactly):
- left, below the track: {{ challenge.start_mrr_formatted }}
- right, below the track: {{ challenge.target_mrr_formatted }}
- progress percent below the track: {{ revenue.target_progress_percent }}%

Position the fill and marker at {{ revenue.target_progress_percent }}% of the track width.

Place the progress percent label directly under the filled portion / marker — horizontally aligned with the thumb, not centered on the full bar. When progress is very small, keep the label near the left fill edge (slightly right of the start label so it stays readable), still under the filled segment — never in the middle of the empty track.

Do not draw a revenue history chart, stacked bars, line chart, or legend.

## Accuracy Rules

This banner contains real financial data.

Therefore:

- Render every supplied number accurately.
- Do not invent revenue values.
- Do not change app names.
- Do not change dates.
- Do not change currencies.
- Do not round values unless the formatted value already contains rounding.
- Do not substitute placeholder values.
- Do not display Jinja variables or braces.
- Do not add additional statistics that were not supplied.
- Do not invent a revenue history chart.

